WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.041 --> 00:00:04.921
If you were trapped in a school and forced
to kill your own teacher, what would you do?

00:00:04.921 --> 00:00:06.965
This creature is not human,

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:11.469
and these kids are going to have to figure
out the most creative of ways to kill it

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:15.306
if they want to survive.
I'm going to break down the mistakes made.

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:20.353
What you should do and how to beat
Koro-Sensei in Assassination's Classroom.

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:23.023
This creature is more than meets the eye.

00:00:23.106 --> 00:00:27.068
This is class three,
and they only have one test that they need

00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:31.489
to pass, kill their teacher,
readying their guns Nagisa here

00:00:31.489 --> 00:00:34.117
and the rest of the class
shoot at Koro-Sensei

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:36.369
while he reads out the roll call
for the morning.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:39.748
This creature has no known weakness,
and these students

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:43.543
are going to have to get pretty damn creative
if they want to beat it.

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:48.214
Class three, also known as the end
class, is the lowest of the low.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:52.010
The students in this class
are the ones who failed of their final exams

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.763
to be able to proceed
into the next stage of high school.

00:00:54.804 --> 00:00:57.891
Now this is their only chance at redemption.

00:00:57.932 --> 00:01:00.935
The classroom is even separated
from the rest of the school

00:01:00.935 --> 00:01:06.316
to further emphasize how damn stupid these
kids are on the very first day of class.

00:01:06.357 --> 00:01:10.570
This strikingly yellow forearmed
creature known as Koro-Sensei, introduces

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:11.946
himself to the students.

00:01:11.946 --> 00:01:15.492
The kids are confused by
what the hell is going on, so this government

00:01:15.492 --> 00:01:20.080
official Karasuma explains that this creature
must be killed for the good of humanity.

00:01:20.121 --> 00:01:23.124
This creature is responsible
for destroying the moon

00:01:23.124 --> 00:01:26.711
and will destroy the Earth
in the same way by March of the next year.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:31.299
This is top secret information, and only the
world's leaders know that the Earth is soon

00:01:31.299 --> 00:01:32.300
going to blow up.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:34.886
He tells the students to keep
this knowledge a secret.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:37.138
Or else they'll face a global panic.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:41.267
Suddenly, the man tries stabbing Koro-Sensei,
but his speed is unmatched.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:44.771
Getting the better of him,
Koro-Sensei takes the time to groom his hair,

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:49.025
while the man explains a little bit
more about their new teacher, Koro-Sensei

00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:53.655
speed maxes out and Mach 20, or roughly
25,000 kilometers per hour.

00:01:53.655 --> 00:01:57.492
This means that he could easily
leave planet Earth before it gets destroyed.

00:01:57.492 --> 00:01:58.660
To combat the creature,

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:02.038
the ministry has produced
a specially made B-BBEE pellets and knives,

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:05.416
which cause extreme damage
when used on Koro-Sensei.

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.669
OK, this guy is no joke.

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:09.295
This is Koro-Sensei,

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:13.675
also known as the world's
deadliest assassin and nicknamed the Reaper.

00:02:13.675 --> 00:02:16.594
Now you might be wondering
what the hell this creature is.

00:02:16.594 --> 00:02:21.641
His entire body is made from anti-matter,
which is a material in the universe

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:23.601
composed from antiparticles.

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:27.772
They have the same mass as ordinary matter,
but have an opposite charge.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:31.901
If we were to see just how powerful
this stuff is, one gram of antimatter

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:35.613
could, in theory, produce
an explosion the size of a nuclear bomb.

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:38.533
Basically, this stuff is made
from highly unstable matter

00:02:38.533 --> 00:02:42.871
and is volatile as hell,
and our teacher is made from this stuff.

00:02:42.871 --> 00:02:47.500
And unfortunately, all of this insane
power comes with even more insane abilities.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.836
This eight legged
teacher is immune to poisons,

00:02:49.836 --> 00:02:53.923
can compress his entire body and energy
into a small, crystallized sphere

00:02:53.923 --> 00:02:57.552
that is impervious to harm
even from a nuclear warhead.

00:02:57.552 --> 00:02:59.345
He can regenerate severed limbs,

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:03.433
possesses superhuman senses and can travel up
to a speed of about Mach 20.

00:03:03.433 --> 00:03:06.769
And this is just the tip of the iceberg
in terms of abilities.

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.771
Needless to say,
we're going to have to approach

00:03:08.771 --> 00:03:11.858
this guy with extreme caution,
and these students

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:16.571
are about to realize that killing him
won't be nearly as easy as they hope.

00:03:16.571 --> 00:03:19.365
Suddenly,
Koro-Sensei grabs the gun out of his hand

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.701
and detaches one of his arms, regrowing it

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.204
nearly instantly
to the shock of every student.

00:03:24.204 --> 00:03:27.165
The man tells them to calm down
and reveals that Koro-Sensei here

00:03:27.165 --> 00:03:30.501
made an agreement with the government
to never hurt the students.

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:32.503
This creature is like no other.

00:03:32.503 --> 00:03:35.340
He tells the students
that he's decided to accept his death

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:39.135
as long as he gets to teach this school's
class three.

00:03:39.177 --> 00:03:41.679
The government doesn't understand
chorus conditions,

00:03:41.679 --> 00:03:44.891
but either way, the government
official informs them that they've put down

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:49.729
a ¥10 billion reward to whichever student
can assassinate the evil teacher.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:54.108
From that point onwards, the kids begin
to realize the severity of the situation

00:03:54.108 --> 00:03:57.195
and begin to train
even harder to kill Koro-Sensei.

00:03:57.195 --> 00:04:00.406
Not only that, though,
Karasuma becomes their assistant teacher

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:03.243
and is joined by a professional assassin
known as Irina.

00:04:03.284 --> 00:04:04.619
She's an absolute badass

00:04:04.619 --> 00:04:09.249
and is great at her job, but not even Irina
can cause a dent in Koro-Sensei's armor.

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:12.335
Failing her mission,
she's demoted to a lowly English teacher

00:04:12.335 --> 00:04:13.753
for the rest of the semester.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:17.674
During lunch break, Nagisa here
shows his classmates a potential weakness

00:04:17.674 --> 00:04:21.094
he found regarding the colors
that Koro-Sensei switches to and from.

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:25.098
Based on his emotions, his friends tell him
it's a worthless piece of information

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:29.477
and get ready to pull another assassination
attempt in the next class, looking worried.

00:04:29.519 --> 00:04:33.523
Nagisa informs Koro-Sensei
that his work is already complete Koro-Sensei

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:36.567
then asks him to give him the work
so he can read it over.

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.945
But Nagisa here has something else in mind.

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:43.408
In a single motion, he tries to stab
Koro-Sensei, but he's too slow.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.742
That's when Nagisa reveals

00:04:44.742 --> 00:04:49.205
a bomb attached to his shirt, blowing up
and taking out the teacher once and for all.

00:04:49.247 --> 00:04:53.584
Thrilled beyond belief, the kids
congratulate themselves on a job well done.

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:56.796
However, one of them notices
the leftover skin when suddenly

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:59.882
the teacher appears on the roof
and tells them that they've been outsmarted.

00:05:00.049 --> 00:05:02.885
He reveals that he sheds his skin
once per month

00:05:02.885 --> 00:05:07.140
and that the old skin took all of the damage,
realizing which students did it

00:05:07.181 --> 00:05:10.310
Koro-Sensei changes colors
and tells the delinquents

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:14.522
that while he's made an agreement
to not hurt anyone in the classroom,

00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:19.068
he can still kill every single one of them
outside of this room.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:22.196
He tells them that they have a lot to learn,
and these students

00:05:22.196 --> 00:05:26.284
are going to have to attempt even crazier
assassinations in the near future.

00:05:26.284 --> 00:05:29.454
The next day, the students have Koro-Sensei
trapped in a net.

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:33.416
one of the students shows the teachers
that he put down a dirty magazine

00:05:33.416 --> 00:05:36.919
exactly where the net was placed,
showing off his intelligence

00:05:36.961 --> 00:05:40.548
when suddenly Koro-Sensei
spent the net over and over until it breaks.

00:05:40.548 --> 00:05:42.759
When the students notice a lapse of focus.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:45.928
They attempt to shoot the teacher,
but they're still too slow.

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:48.514
Koro-Sensei
simply swings himself onto the roof,

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:52.769
where he tells everyone that he'll be
doubling everyone's homework as punishment.

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:57.315
Okay, this guy is a horny bastard,
but then our very own anime writer.

00:05:57.315 --> 00:05:57.982
Sorry, Tom,

00:05:57.982 --> 00:06:00.568
and this is a case
example of why it's imperative

00:06:00.568 --> 00:06:02.737
that we plan our moves more carefully

00:06:02.737 --> 00:06:05.365
and that we should always have
a backup plan in place.

00:06:05.365 --> 00:06:07.450
Because if we notice with Koro-Sensei,

00:06:07.492 --> 00:06:11.788
he'll almost always be able to foil
our first plan, a assassination attempt.

00:06:11.788 --> 00:06:15.750
But what if we had a contingent Plan B
and a Plan C and a Plan D?

00:06:15.750 --> 00:06:16.959
You get my point.

00:06:16.959 --> 00:06:18.252
We need to plan ahead enough

00:06:18.252 --> 00:06:22.423
so that this anti-matter, education
loving monster doesn't know what hits him.

00:06:22.465 --> 00:06:24.592
An example
of how we could have had a backup plan

00:06:24.592 --> 00:06:27.553
after the initial assassination attempt
could have been in the form

00:06:27.553 --> 00:06:29.847
of when we caught Koro-Sensei in the net.

00:06:29.847 --> 00:06:33.768
After he got caught, he broke off
the basketball rim and landed on the roof.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.479
Now, if these kids thought ahead in advance,
they could have gauged

00:06:36.479 --> 00:06:39.273
that the distance
from where Koro-Sensei and the roof was

00:06:39.315 --> 00:06:41.609
was close enough
that he could have made the jump

00:06:41.609 --> 00:06:43.861
and that the roof, in comparison
to anywhere else,

00:06:43.861 --> 00:06:48.199
was probably the safest platform to land on
and high enough that no other students

00:06:48.199 --> 00:06:50.660
could come close to him if we planned ahead.

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:52.537
They could have tried
placing a bomb on the roof

00:06:52.537 --> 00:06:53.788
or left some students in

00:06:53.788 --> 00:06:58.167
and around the roof area, with the government
issued anti sensei weapons ready to go.

00:06:58.167 --> 00:07:00.753
This is an example
of how having a Plan B in place

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:03.756
could have potentially worked,
and there are a myriad of ways

00:07:03.756 --> 00:07:08.094
that the students can incorporate this level
of thinking into all of their future

00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:09.595
assassination attempts.

00:07:09.595 --> 00:07:13.391
That's when this cool looking kid
named Karma appears on the scene.

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:16.769
He and Koro-Sensei introduce themselves
by sharing a handshake

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:19.689
when suddenly Koro-Sensei
pulls his hand in pain.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:23.734
Karma scolds him and reveals that he's
attached multiple knives to his hand.

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:27.113
This kid is smart,
and the only reason he's in this class

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:30.366
is because of his violent behavior
in the year before.

00:07:30.366 --> 00:07:36.330
In the classroom, Koro-Sensei notices a dead
octopus on one of the tables outing himself.

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:39.417
Karma tells the teacher
he killed it, thinking it was him.

00:07:39.417 --> 00:07:41.127
This angers Koro-Sensei,

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:43.963
who promises to show him
the extent of his abilities

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:47.383
by sticking a flaming hot takoyaki
into his mouth.

00:07:47.425 --> 00:07:48.718
Later on, he and Nagisa

00:07:48.718 --> 00:07:53.139
have a conversation about their new teacher
discussing who the hell he actually is.

00:07:53.139 --> 00:07:57.852
Suddenly, Koro-Sensei shows up out of nowhere
to inform Karma that one of his goals is to

00:07:57.852 --> 00:08:02.523
improve the skills of his assassin students,
adding that he's been taking good care of.

00:08:02.523 --> 00:08:05.943
Based on today's events,
Karma asks him whether or not he'd

00:08:05.943 --> 00:08:10.031
risk his life to save his student,
to which the teacher confirms he would.

00:08:10.072 --> 00:08:14.285
Hearing this, the student whips out
a gun and jumps off the nearby cliff.

00:08:14.327 --> 00:08:17.330
If Koro-Sensei comes to his rescue,
he'll be shot dead

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:22.043
by Karma's gun, and if he doesn't, he'll lose
his reputation as a teacher forever.

00:08:22.043 --> 00:08:25.546
Without hesitation,
Koro-Sensei creates a massive spiderweb,

00:08:25.546 --> 00:08:28.841
which breaks his fall
while keeping the student immobilized.

00:08:28.883 --> 00:08:33.971
The students plants are ruined again, but
he promises that he'll kill him someday soon.

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:36.724
OK, these two guys here
failed in an epic way.

00:08:36.766 --> 00:08:41.729
I bet Karma didn't think of the fact that if
Koro-Sensei tried to save him at max speed,

00:08:41.729 --> 00:08:42.813
he would have been dead.

00:08:42.813 --> 00:08:46.734
And if Karma did manage to kill Koro-Sensei,
he'd also die from the fall.

00:08:46.734 --> 00:08:50.071
And to top that off,
Karma did and utilized Nagasaki at all

00:08:50.071 --> 00:08:52.615
and just had him standing there
like a chump .

00:08:52.615 --> 00:08:55.618
two dudes with one half baked plan.
And you know what?

00:08:55.660 --> 00:09:00.164
I'll go out on a limb and say that
even if we added 100 more dudes to this plan,

00:09:00.206 --> 00:09:02.708
the only thing we would have had
is an all out disaster.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.252
Because yet again, these kids

00:09:04.252 --> 00:09:08.798
failed to pick up on the breadcrumb clues
that our favorite teacher has left for us,

00:09:08.798 --> 00:09:12.760
and that is his love for the obscene
portrayal of the opposite sex.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:13.803
I would have swapped out

00:09:13.803 --> 00:09:17.515
useless Nagisa for blond baddie
Irina and would have told her to use

00:09:17.515 --> 00:09:19.767
her feminine ways to lure Koro-Sensei

00:09:19.767 --> 00:09:22.395
into letting his guard down
for the sake of humanity.

00:09:22.436 --> 00:09:23.145
Of course,

00:09:23.145 --> 00:09:25.606
all they would have to do
is just flirt with him a little bit

00:09:25.606 --> 00:09:28.943
and let his guard down before
blasting a hole right through his brain.

00:09:28.985 --> 00:09:30.778
This way we would have stood a better chance

00:09:30.778 --> 00:09:33.614
and we could have carried out this plan
with much better results.

00:09:33.698 --> 00:09:35.616
Meanwhile, at the Ministry of Defense,

00:09:35.616 --> 00:09:38.160
the government officials
worry about the fate of the Earth.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.705
There's seemingly nothing
that can stop this creature,

00:09:40.705 --> 00:09:45.084
and if nothing can be done,
the entire planet will be destroyed by March.

00:09:45.126 --> 00:09:48.462
The order official scolds the teacher
for not being able to do anything,

00:09:48.462 --> 00:09:53.009
but informs him that they'll be sending in a
transfer student as the next line of attack.

00:09:53.009 --> 00:09:56.137
The next day, Karasuma introduces
a new student.

00:09:56.178 --> 00:09:58.264
However, she's not like the others.

00:09:58.264 --> 00:09:59.765
She's a female, a high.

00:09:59.765 --> 00:10:04.353
Robot shaped like a box
whose sole purpose is to take out Koro-Sensei

00:10:04.353 --> 00:10:05.646
the air robots suddenly

00:10:05.646 --> 00:10:10.276
reveals a dozen machine guns from both sides
and start shooting at Koro-Sensei .

00:10:10.276 --> 00:10:15.197
However, even the latest military technology
is no match for his speed after class,

00:10:15.197 --> 00:10:16.866
one of the students scores the A.I.

00:10:16.866 --> 00:10:19.493
for creating such a mess
with all of her bullets.

00:10:19.535 --> 00:10:20.578
And that's when it begins

00:10:20.578 --> 00:10:25.583
to calculate the percentage of success
for killing Koro-Sensei before graduation,

00:10:25.583 --> 00:10:30.463
revealing a number of 90.4%
during the next class.

00:10:30.504 --> 00:10:32.798
The students wrapped chains around the robot

00:10:32.798 --> 00:10:35.801
to avoid cleaning up her bullets
every time she fires.

00:10:35.801 --> 00:10:38.846
When classes
finished, Koro-Sensei approaches the A.I.

00:10:38.846 --> 00:10:41.807
and tells her to try getting along
with her fellow classmates.

00:10:41.807 --> 00:10:45.311
The AI is confused as to how to do that,
so Koro-Sensei reveals

00:10:45.311 --> 00:10:49.815
that he's compiled data from all of Class
three students into these textbooks.

00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:54.153
He unlocks her chains, and that night
the robot begins processing the information.

00:10:54.153 --> 00:10:56.822
The next day, the air appears on everyone's
phones,

00:10:56.864 --> 00:11:00.785
revealing that she made herself an app
to be able to communicate with each student

00:11:00.785 --> 00:11:03.996
and support their assassination plans
in the classroom.

00:11:03.996 --> 00:11:06.374
The students decide
to give her the name Rita,

00:11:06.374 --> 00:11:08.709
and she soon becomes friendly
with everyone there.

00:11:08.709 --> 00:11:10.294
The students mentioned that there will be

00:11:10.294 --> 00:11:14.590
another transfer student coming in,
and that's when Koro-Sensei enters the room

00:11:14.590 --> 00:11:16.008
for the morning roll call.

00:11:16.008 --> 00:11:18.594
Suddenly,
a kid falls from the roof and immediately

00:11:18.594 --> 00:11:21.430
sits down,
while a mysterious man draped in white enters

00:11:21.430 --> 00:11:25.518
the classroom and scores the kid named Itona
for not coming in the proper way.

00:11:25.559 --> 00:11:29.897
The man apologizes for his actions
and introduces himself as his guardian.

00:11:29.939 --> 00:11:32.525
Itona
then gets up and grabs Karma by the hair,

00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:37.363
telling him that he might be the strongest
in the class right now, but not anymore.

00:11:37.405 --> 00:11:41.701
He confronts Koro-Sensei and states
that he is the only one worthy to beat

00:11:41.701 --> 00:11:46.706
in this room, insisting that they face off
in this classroom straight after school,

00:11:46.747 --> 00:11:48.374
setting up a makeshift arena.

00:11:48.374 --> 00:11:51.877
The two face off
and the assassination attempt begins. Itokawa

00:11:51.877 --> 00:11:56.132
feels tentacles of his own, which angers
Koro-Sensei on the very first exchange.

00:11:56.173 --> 00:11:58.384
The teacher reverts to the classic roof
trick,

00:11:58.426 --> 00:12:00.594
showing that Itona here is no pushover.

00:12:00.594 --> 00:12:02.972
The little kid manages to cut off
Koro-Sensei's

00:12:02.972 --> 00:12:05.141
tentacles, reducing his speed dramatically.

00:12:05.141 --> 00:12:10.271
Now the probability of him dying from
the next attack has increased by 60%.

00:12:10.312 --> 00:12:13.566
Koro-Sensei laughs it off
and the little kid goes to finish them off.

00:12:13.566 --> 00:12:18.195
Suddenly, one of his tentacles is cut off
by an antisense a knife, reducing his powers,

00:12:18.195 --> 00:12:20.030
wrapping Itona up in his own skin.

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:23.242
He throws the kid out of the classroom
and ends at the assassination.

00:12:23.242 --> 00:12:26.954
The man in white takes him away,
promising to come back for revenge.

00:12:26.954 --> 00:12:31.208
OK, Itona was the one foe who may have stood
a chance against Koro-Sensei

00:12:31.208 --> 00:12:35.254
as he has tentacles of his own and incredible
physical abilities on par with him.

00:12:35.254 --> 00:12:39.341
But he made the crucial mistake of doing
what Koro-Sensei expected him to do,

00:12:39.341 --> 00:12:43.137
which was to play fair
because while they faced off fair and square,

00:12:43.179 --> 00:12:47.641
Itona missed the opportunity to create
a coordinated attack with his schoolmates

00:12:47.641 --> 00:12:51.437
and missed a chance where teamwork could have
prevailed over simply working alone.

00:12:51.479 --> 00:12:55.107
Remember now
